AWS Service Examples
- EC2: The customer patches and hardens the operating system, configures Security Groups, manages IAM roles, and secures applications.
- RDS: AWS manages much of the underlying infrastructure and database engine maintenance, depending on the service configuration. Customers still manage database access, encryption choices, parameter settings, and network exposure.
- Lambda: AWS manages the infrastructure and execution environment; customers secure function code, permissions, secrets, and logging.
- S3: AWS secures the underlying infrastructure; customers configure bucket policies and access controls, public-access settings, encryption, and data lifecycle controls.
